@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000/api

### =========================
### Login Admin
### =========================
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ismael@email.com",
  "password": "Test1234!"
}


### Capturar tokens automáticamente
@accessToken = {{login.response.body.access_token}}
@refreshToken = {{login.response.body.refresh_token}}


### =========================================================================
### FLUJO COMPLETO: crear proyecto -> subir + clasificar (manual, CSRT-) ->
### esperar a que termine -> generar Excel -> descargar.
### Archivo real: processing/proceso-metrados-base/archives/CUS ET2 ST1 EST
### BIM 5A ZZZ 1001.ifc (109MB, 26141 elementos) — el procesamiento tarda
### varios minutos, no es instantáneo.
### =========================================================================

### 1. Crear el proyecto
# @name createProject
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "CUS ET2 - Prueba exportación Excel",
  "description": null,
  "location": "Cusco, Perú",
  "client": null,
  "contractor": null,
  "start_date": null,
  "end_date": null
}


### Capturar el project_id recién creado
@createdProjectId = {{createProject.response.body.project_id}}


### 2. Subir + procesar en modo MANUAL — classification_override va como
### JSON.stringify(...) en un campo de texto (multipart), mismo patrón que
### specialty_id. specialty_id es obligatorio acá porque no hay
### replaces_ifc_document_id (esto crea un ifc_documents nuevo).
### ⚠️ Tarda varios minutos en terminar — este POST responde 202 casi al
### instante, el procesamiento real sigue en background (ver request 4).
# @name processIfc
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{createdProjectId}}/ifc-metrados/process
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="specialty_id"

2
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="document_name"

CUS ET2 ST1 EST
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="classification_override"

{"mode":"manual","property_prefix":"CSRT-","code_property_set":"Otros","code_property_name":"CSRT-Partida1","description_property_set":"Otros","description_property_name":"CSRT-DescripcionPartida1","unit_property_set":"Otros","unit_property_name":"CSRT-Unidad1"}
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="CUS_ET2.ifc"
Content-Type: application/octet-stream

< ../../processing/proceso-metrados-base/archives/CUS ET2 ST1 EST BIM 5A ZZZ 1001.ifc
--WebAppBoundary--


### Capturar el ifc_file_id devuelto
@ifcFileId = {{processIfc.response.body.ifc_file_id}}


### 3. Consultar el estado del procesamiento (polling) — volvé a correr
### este request cada 30-60s hasta que "status" pase de "processing" a
### "done" (o "error") antes de seguir con el paso 4.
GET {{baseUrl}}/ifc-files/{{ifcFileId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


### 4. Generar el Excel — solo corré esto cuando el request 3 de arriba
### ya muestre "status": "done". Guarda un archivo real
### (file_type='excel', generated_from_ifc_file_id = {{ifcFileId}}).
# @name exportExcel
POST {{baseUrl}}/ifc-files/63/export-excel
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


### Capturar el file_id del Excel recién generado
@exportedExcelFileId = {{exportExcel.response.body.file_id}}


### 5. Descargar el Excel generado
GET {{baseUrl}}/files/{{exportedExcelFileId}}/content?download=true
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
